Z||000018||Scott2M4||11-19-1999||04:52 AM||||I'll take a stab at CAGS.  I don't know what the acronym stands for (something like Computerized Automatic Gear Selector) but I -BELIEVE- it's the mechanism in the Vette/Camaro/Firebird 6-speed that forces you to shift from 1st to 4th gear when the RPMs don't reach a certain level (i.e. you're probably driving through town).  It's supposedly a way of getting better gas mileage out of these beasts.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Carrolles||11-19-1999||06:59 AM||||Here is what my '85 Helms manual says about the Shift Light for the v-6<P>"The shift light indicates the best transmission shift point for maximum fuel economy.  The light is controlled by the ECM and is turned on by grounding CKT 456."<P>The schematic doesn't give me a clue as to what controls this.||||reg||1
Z||000020||DJRice||11-19-1999||09:02 AM||||I think your right on the CAGS thing.  I had a friend in college that had a 300+ HP LT1 Z28 bought off Dale Earnhardts Chevy lot in S.C.  That car way fast and had that skip shift deal.  Technically speaking, I think its kind of a neat idea, but I could understand where it would be a pain to some people.||||reg||1
Z||000021||deceler8||11-19-1999||10:19 AM||||The V6 guys should have lights that say something like "SHIFT ALREADY" or "Pardon me, Mister Hot Rodder, but it's time to shift".<P>How about altering the light to display the shift point for chirping the tires ?<P>CHIRP||||reg||1
Z||000022||RossT||11-19-1999||10:33 AM||||All this talk talk about the upshift indicator light got me thinking about my 88gt.  I was sure that I did not have one. I rushed home from work and opened up my 88 owners manual.  Sure enough on page 2c-2 the optional gage cluster showes the shift indicator above the right turn signal indicator!!!!!  BUT, on page 2-11 under starting and operating i found SHIFT INDICATOR LIGHT: "If your Fiero has a manual transaxle and an L4 engine, a SHIFT light on the instrument panel. This light will show you when to upshift for best fuel economy at any acceleration." But I have the GT, Since I don't have the L4, I must not have the Light?  So I did the next thing, I pulled the cover of my hibernating beast.  Took a very bright trouble light, and put it close to the gage cluster.  NO UPSHIFT LIGHT. IT WAS BLANK, along with two of the other small rectangular boxes.  since Batboy has it in his GT, it must have been droped in later modles.  Please correct me if I am wrong.<P><BR>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000023||deceler8||11-19-1999||10:54 AM||||I think the "shift light" is buried in the automotive bad idea graveyard right next to Chrysler's "talking cars".||||reg||1
Z||000024||fiero56||11-19-1999||11:03 AM||||My Formula doesn't have the light either. Maybe they took it out of the v-6 with the restyle of the GT in '86.  Just a gues, but it works for me.||||reg||10
Z||000025||88GT||11-19-1999||12:49 PM||||I had an 87 GT for a while and it didn't have one either.||||reg||3
Z||000026||Rodrv6||11-19-1999||02:19 PM||||Here is another use for the upshift light at least on the four cylinder (TBI) engines. If you are driving in one of the lower gears and the light comes on, release the accelerator pedal COMPLETELY and the light is supposed to go out.  If it stays on, this is the first sign that the throttle position sensor is on its way out.  Mine has done this several times over the years and within a few months of it first happening the TPS gets bad enough to set a code.  I seem to get about 18 months or so to a TPS!||||reg||3
Z||000027||batboy||11-19-1999||04:52 PM||||Oh guano, you mean I might be wrong AGAIN!<P>Does anyone with a later model GT or 6 cylinder SE have a shift light? My 87 SE with an automatic and 2.5 has the shift light on the dash, of course it has never lit up since it's an automatic, but it's there.||||reg||1
Z||000028||JMergen||11-19-1999||11:08 PM||||My 86 SE 2.8 4spd has the shift indicator.I figure if its not on, Im not driving.||||reg||1
